WEBVTT

00:02.410 --> 00:05.380
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.480 --> 00:08.840
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.100 --> 00:10.640
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.480 --> 00:13.250
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.350 --> 00:17.080
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.190 --> 00:20.020
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.390 --> 00:22.020
They are also known as...

00:22.260 --> 00:24.700
the Shinigami.

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
nureta hitomi no oku

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.420 --> 00:42.670
Yami no Matsuei

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
azayaka na sekai wa

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
The splendid world

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
A new era beckons now

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
The injured black wings

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
The crimson kiss

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:17.110 --> 02:19.540
<i>A Shinigami is after me.</i>

02:20.080 --> 02:21.370
Good morning.

02:22.080 --> 02:25.810
<i>Considering I'm already being
ostracized because of Maki's death...</i>

02:30.090 --> 02:31.180
Please feel free.

02:31.290 --> 02:33.080
No, thank you.

02:35.790 --> 02:39.390
<i>They follow me night and day!</i>

02:42.930 --> 02:44.800
Can I sit with you?

02:50.010 --> 02:52.300
<i>This is turning into a living hell.</i>

02:52.410 --> 02:54.240
Back in the Meiji Period

02:54.340 --> 02:59.250
it was a daily occurrence for a man
to be attacked on the streets at night.

02:59.350 --> 03:02.320
It would be all over the newspapers.

03:02.420 --> 03:05.050
You sure know a lot of strange stuff, teacher.

03:05.150 --> 03:08.780
Well, I was born just around that time...

03:10.690 --> 03:14.250
Teacher, never mind your idle chatter!
Let's get on with class!

03:14.760 --> 03:16.060
I'm sorry.

03:16.170 --> 03:19.190
Teacher, your little brother's pushing you around.

03:21.200 --> 03:25.160
<i>Why do they laugh so much?
These guys are Shinigami.</i>

03:25.240 --> 03:30.210
Episode 12: The Kyoto Arc, Part 3

03:37.050 --> 03:41.610
<i>They pretend to be human.
They pretend to be normal teachers.</i>

03:41.820 --> 03:45.690
<i>They're watching me.
They want to kill me.</i>

03:57.240 --> 03:59.000
- Are you all right?
- Ikaruga!

03:59.610 --> 04:01.240
What do you want?!

04:02.810 --> 04:05.680
What are you saying I did?!
Who are you people?!

04:05.950 --> 04:09.080
Maki getting killed like that,
and all this happening to me...

04:09.190 --> 04:11.850
It's all because of you and that doctor!

04:11.950 --> 04:14.790
I want my best friend back!
I want Maki back!

04:14.890 --> 04:16.590
You evil demon!

04:20.700 --> 04:22.430
Don't worry about it.

04:22.530 --> 04:27.160
I don't care what she calls me
as long as I can protect her.

04:27.540 --> 04:29.500
That's what I've decided.

04:39.550 --> 04:42.280
Saki, do you remember?

04:43.220 --> 04:46.280
The time when you first came to my house?

04:49.490 --> 04:53.020
I remember clearly as if it was only yesterday.

04:53.130 --> 04:57.960
That day when the devil
descended before me.

05:01.000 --> 05:04.300
<i>Kazutaka, this boy is your older brother.</i>

05:04.410 --> 05:05.930
<i>Nice to meet you, Kazutaka.</i>

05:06.310 --> 05:09.540
A step-brother, a little older than me, Shido Saki .

05:09.650 --> 05:11.910
I had a sibling like that.

05:12.620 --> 05:14.980
What I couldn't forgive the most

05:15.080 --> 05:18.140
is that on the day I received
life in my mother's womb,

05:18.250 --> 05:21.880
my father had already
impregnated another woman.

05:22.860 --> 05:25.550
Regardless, Saki...

05:25.660 --> 05:28.630
I tried my best to get along with you.

05:28.730 --> 05:33.190
The man who caused this is the one to blame.

05:34.170 --> 05:35.430
But you...

05:36.410 --> 05:37.870
<i>Poor thing.</i>

05:37.970 --> 05:40.410
<i>First it's his father, and now his mother.</i>

05:40.510 --> 05:44.610
<i>One of those "mysterious deaths."
How creepy.</i>

05:47.680 --> 05:50.740
You were laughing back then.

05:51.220 --> 05:53.710
Like the first time that we had met.

05:54.220 --> 05:57.920
That's when I knew the true
meaning of that derision.

06:03.830 --> 06:05.060
<i>Saki...!</i>

06:06.640 --> 06:09.370
<i>Were you the one who killed them?!</i>

06:14.080 --> 06:15.540
<i>You bastard!</i>

06:27.660 --> 06:28.780
<i>Young Master.</i>

06:31.730 --> 06:33.250
<i>Sakaki...</i>

06:34.360 --> 06:37.460
You took everything away from me.

06:40.840 --> 06:45.210
These past 16 years,
I've lived only to finish you off.

06:45.510 --> 06:49.440
Soon I will have a body for you.

06:52.410 --> 06:55.940
This time I'll kill you
with my own two hands!

07:14.600 --> 07:18.200
<i>Take a look at a newspaper
if you want to know. Bye.</i>

07:18.230 --> 07:22.940
Serial Killer on the loose!!

07:18.310 --> 07:22.800
I received the sample hair
two days after the murder.

07:22.980 --> 07:25.640
Muraki-kun couldn't have...

07:29.850 --> 07:31.050
Muraki-kun!

07:32.250 --> 07:35.090
Doctor, about that specimen.

07:35.190 --> 07:37.720
- Did you get him?!
- It's not so easy.

07:37.830 --> 07:38.790
I see.

07:38.890 --> 07:40.890
However, I've set a trap.

07:41.000 --> 07:42.020
Trap?

07:42.130 --> 07:44.070
Can I count on your help?

07:44.470 --> 07:46.930
It's nothing difficult.

07:47.040 --> 07:52.240
There's only a little more to go
until you take the world by storm.

07:53.140 --> 07:54.940
That's right...

08:05.590 --> 08:07.110
You evil demon!

08:10.230 --> 08:11.590
Are you all right, teacher?

08:11.690 --> 08:13.180
You should go to the infirmary.

08:13.300 --> 08:15.060
I'm fine. It's just a scratch.

08:15.160 --> 08:17.560
No. I must take you to the infirmary.

08:17.670 --> 08:19.100
Hey, that's not fair!

08:19.200 --> 08:23.000
- I'm taking him!
- I am! I am!

08:23.110 --> 08:24.070
<i>Fools...</i>

08:24.120 --> 08:29.130
Infirmary Room

08:29.450 --> 08:33.400
I at least have to pretend, or
they'll give me a lot of grief later.

08:33.520 --> 08:36.510
Excuse me. Can I get a band-aid?

08:40.520 --> 08:42.920
Well, Tsuzuki-san.
What's the matter?

08:43.030 --> 08:44.420
Muraki!

08:44.530 --> 08:47.930
I'm standing in for the doctor on duty here.

08:48.560 --> 08:51.060
I didn't kill him.

08:51.170 --> 08:53.100
I wish you wouldn't look so angry.

08:55.440 --> 08:59.200
By the way, are you free tonight, Tsuzuki-san?

08:59.840 --> 09:02.210
I have tickets to a Noh performance.

09:02.310 --> 09:03.800
Would you like to come with me?

09:03.910 --> 09:05.440
What are you up to?

09:07.750 --> 09:09.380
<i>Ikaruga Mariko san...</i>

09:09.490 --> 09:11.390
<i>we have a message from your mother.</i>

09:11.490 --> 09:14.250
<i>Please come to the office right away.</i>

09:19.190 --> 09:20.680
<i>That voice!</i>

09:21.160 --> 09:22.790
<i>Dr. Satomi!</i>

09:23.700 --> 09:27.230
You really don't have a choice
in the matter, Tsuzuki-san.

09:28.300 --> 09:29.860
If you refuse...

09:29.970 --> 09:33.240
that poor little Mariko-san will die.

09:33.880 --> 09:36.170
What're you talking about?!
Hisoka's watching over--

09:36.280 --> 09:38.110
They got her!

09:38.210 --> 09:40.080
What?!

09:43.050 --> 09:44.380
Muraki...!

10:00.570 --> 10:02.200
You promised.

10:02.300 --> 10:04.700
Don't you lay a finger on her.

10:04.810 --> 10:08.870
Yes. But only if you honestly
answer my questions.

10:09.880 --> 10:14.380
Note: Momiji-gari means "Mapple leaves viewing".

10:09.880 --> 10:11.440
Momiji-gari, eh?

10:11.550 --> 10:14.380
A performance perfect for the season.

10:16.320 --> 10:18.790
Taira Koremochi, who received an Imperial Order

10:18.890 --> 10:22.450
confronts a demon that terrifies
people at an autumn banquet.

10:22.560 --> 10:24.550
This is the fifth.

10:25.160 --> 10:27.920
I don't care to listen to
your stupid interpretation.

10:28.030 --> 10:30.660
This Noh performance was just
to draw me out, wasn't it?

10:30.770 --> 10:34.070
Tell me!
Why did you draw me out?!

10:35.500 --> 10:38.500
It emerged out of my grandfather's belongings.

10:39.010 --> 10:42.270
This is a picture of you 72 years ago.

10:42.380 --> 10:44.440
I don't remember...

10:44.750 --> 10:46.940
I can't blame you for not remembering.

10:47.050 --> 10:50.110
Back then you were
incapable of rational thought.

10:51.120 --> 10:54.950
With the exception of
regaining consciousness once

10:55.060 --> 11:00.390
without water, food or sleep,
you managed to stave off death.

11:00.500 --> 11:02.620
That's a lie.
I don't believe it!

11:02.730 --> 11:05.760
Those beautiful purple eyes of yours...

11:06.900 --> 11:10.030
A color that one never sees in human eyes.

11:11.240 --> 11:15.010
After looking over the materials
left behind by my grandfather,

11:15.110 --> 11:19.210
I found genetic information
there that was not human.

11:20.820 --> 11:25.550
I'm sure you also feel it somewhat.
Some special quality about you.

11:26.420 --> 11:28.390
A body that does not deteriorate.

11:28.490 --> 11:30.820
You can never die from any wound.

11:34.800 --> 11:36.590
Now, Tsuzuki-san.

11:38.170 --> 11:41.000
What are you?

11:43.610 --> 11:45.770
Are you really human?

11:59.790 --> 12:02.260
Tsuzuki-san, you are...

12:03.760 --> 12:07.220
a monster with the blood of a demon.

12:13.400 --> 12:17.360
I've long had a dream
that can never be fulfilled.

12:26.950 --> 12:31.410
Yami no Matsuei

12:34.490 --> 12:35.820
What do you mean?

12:35.920 --> 12:38.950
Just as I said, this is the end of our association.

12:39.060 --> 12:40.150
What are you talking about?!

12:40.260 --> 12:44.200
I'm sure the experiment will work
with that man's immortal cells!

12:44.300 --> 12:45.600
It's okay now.

12:45.700 --> 12:48.170
I already have the bait to draw him out.

12:48.270 --> 12:50.470
- You tricked me!
- How unfortunate.

12:50.710 --> 12:53.700
I was more interested in cloning research

12:53.810 --> 12:58.140
for transplanting body parts
rather than creating a human body.

12:58.480 --> 13:01.420
However, your research
did not progress that way.

13:02.220 --> 13:06.650
Besides, your vainglorious
indulgences have changed you.

13:06.760 --> 13:08.280
What's wrong with that?!

13:08.390 --> 13:10.950
Eventually my research
will become standard!

13:11.060 --> 13:12.360
Head, hands, organs...

13:12.460 --> 13:15.830
What's wrong with creating
body parts for the body?!

13:15.930 --> 13:18.960
This is research that will benefit mankind!

13:19.070 --> 13:20.800
For mankind?

13:20.900 --> 13:24.570
I suppose that's the basis
of our fundamental difference.

13:24.670 --> 13:28.440
For you, medicine is aimed at
improving the human state.

13:28.980 --> 13:32.780
My research is aimed at killing humans.

13:32.880 --> 13:35.110
Y-You're insane...!

13:37.620 --> 13:39.180
Have you finally realized?

13:39.290 --> 13:41.380
Did you kill them all?

13:42.060 --> 13:45.420
You said that you'd collected
from the bodies that had no kin.

13:45.990 --> 13:50.430
I'm going to have you die and
take all of the blame with you.

13:57.640 --> 13:59.730
Good bye, Doctor.

14:05.650 --> 14:09.810
Tsuzuki-san, I will return her as promised.

14:20.860 --> 14:25.600
Hey, Hisoka.
Sorry for dragging you out here.

14:25.930 --> 14:28.800
I wouldn't want you
falling into a gutter after all.

14:28.900 --> 14:30.370
Here you go.

14:31.170 --> 14:32.270
Thanks.

14:32.910 --> 14:35.710
Hey, you've had too much.

14:38.280 --> 14:43.380
Hey, Hisoka, apparently I'm not human.

14:45.050 --> 14:47.390
Then, what does that make me?

14:47.490 --> 14:48.580
Tsuzuki...

14:48.690 --> 14:51.720
If I'm not human, then...

14:52.330 --> 14:53.990
who am I?

15:01.870 --> 15:03.740
What're you talking about?

15:03.840 --> 15:07.000
When I was a kid, I got teased a lot.

15:07.110 --> 15:10.740
I was different from everyone...
Different from everything...

15:10.850 --> 15:13.840
They said I wasn't human.

15:15.850 --> 15:17.150
Tsuzuki!

15:20.760 --> 15:22.090
Tsuzuki!

15:22.360 --> 15:24.350
You fool!

15:26.330 --> 15:28.420
Hey! Stop that!

15:31.300 --> 15:34.170
<i>Th-This is... Tsuzuki's past.</i>

15:35.070 --> 15:38.400
<i>Discrimination, persecution, loneliness...</i>

15:38.510 --> 15:41.530
<i>guilt for being alive.</i>

15:42.110 --> 15:45.910
I always knew I was
different from other people.

15:46.750 --> 15:49.910
You were beaten up so badly that time.

15:50.020 --> 15:54.350
But I just wanted to be one of them.

15:54.460 --> 15:57.250
I just wanted to be human.

16:03.230 --> 16:06.830
You are a human being.
I guarantee it.

16:06.940 --> 16:09.100
Hisoka...

16:10.040 --> 16:13.300
You've always been a human being.

16:14.480 --> 16:16.340
So, don't cry anymore.

16:27.090 --> 16:29.180
- Hisoka.
- What?

16:29.290 --> 16:31.190
Am I human?

16:31.290 --> 16:33.960
Yeah. You're human.

16:34.730 --> 16:37.720
Right. I'm human...

16:46.170 --> 16:47.570
Ikaruga?

16:52.210 --> 16:54.150
She'll be fine.

16:54.380 --> 16:56.910
She'll wake up eventually.

16:57.020 --> 16:57.990
Thank goodness.

16:58.390 --> 17:00.680
I think we should keep her here for a while.

17:00.790 --> 17:01.950
Yeah.

17:02.060 --> 17:03.020
What is it?

17:03.120 --> 17:06.920
I'll stay with her tonight,
so you can all get some rest.

17:07.030 --> 17:08.660
Are you sure?

17:09.660 --> 17:14.260
I'd like to stay close to
Mariko-chan at least this one night.

17:14.840 --> 17:16.170
I see.

17:26.820 --> 17:28.750
<i>No one will kill you.</i>

17:29.180 --> 17:31.180
<i>I'll be sure to protect you.</i>

17:38.590 --> 17:39.690
<i>Tsuzuki...</i>

17:54.910 --> 17:56.840
<i>Open your eyes.</i>

17:59.650 --> 18:01.980
<i>The one who tormented you...</i>

18:03.150 --> 18:06.120
<i>Kill the one you detest.</i>

18:28.480 --> 18:29.600
Ikaruga?!

18:32.150 --> 18:33.410
It seems that...

18:33.520 --> 18:37.820
Muraki wants to use Tsuzuki-san's
body for a genetic experiment.

18:37.920 --> 18:38.890
I see.

18:38.990 --> 18:42.510
That old man Satomi
probably got duped by Muraki.

18:42.620 --> 18:45.250
We'd better protect him
or Muraki will do him in.

18:45.360 --> 18:47.490
Right. We'll deal with it first thing.

18:47.600 --> 18:51.460
Please. He could be a very
important witness as well.

18:52.270 --> 18:53.730
What's going on?!

18:55.040 --> 18:56.900
Stop it! I said stop it!

18:58.810 --> 19:00.500
Stop it! Please stop!

19:03.410 --> 19:05.310
Stop!

19:06.250 --> 19:09.270
<i>Please stop. I don't want to
hurt anyone anymore.</i>

19:10.220 --> 19:12.410
<i>Anyone...</i>

19:27.240 --> 19:32.170
To protect our master is the duty of us Shinigami.

19:32.640 --> 19:35.870
Stop it, Suzaku.
Muraki is manipulating that girl!

19:35.980 --> 19:40.310
- Get back!
- Purify your soul with my fire!

19:40.620 --> 19:41.880
I'll lead the way!

19:44.950 --> 19:46.280
Stop it!

19:49.720 --> 19:51.020
It's hot!

19:51.730 --> 19:53.280
I can't breathe!

19:53.960 --> 19:57.130
Help me! Murderer!

20:06.410 --> 20:08.770
What the hell's going on?!

20:10.310 --> 20:11.710
Kurosaki?

20:15.150 --> 20:17.550
He's lost his mind.

20:17.650 --> 20:19.050
Tsuzuki!

20:19.490 --> 20:20.550
Watch it!

20:28.500 --> 20:29.690
It's trying to intimidate.

20:29.800 --> 20:31.700
Like a parent bird does
to protect its offspring.

20:31.800 --> 20:33.130
What...?

20:33.230 --> 20:35.500
But Tsuzuki's right there!

20:35.600 --> 20:37.200
<i>I've died again.</i>

20:38.110 --> 20:39.970
<i>Nothing changes.</i>

20:41.080 --> 20:42.340
<i>It's too late...</i>

20:42.440 --> 20:43.670
Tsuzuki...!

20:44.110 --> 20:45.580
<i>Thank you.</i>

20:47.680 --> 20:49.150
- Hold it!
- No!

20:49.250 --> 20:52.080
He's leaving us, Tatsumi-san!

20:54.960 --> 20:56.450
What's this?

21:07.600 --> 21:09.090
Muraki!

21:18.850 --> 21:21.710
Tsuzuki... Tsuzuki...

21:22.050 --> 21:23.480
Tsuzuki...

21:26.020 --> 21:29.220
Tsuzuki!

21:40.460 --> 21:43.510
Next Episode

21:42.370 --> 21:44.340
He could not die.

21:44.540 --> 21:46.370
He could not save.

21:47.010 --> 21:50.070
Tormented by his own past...

21:50.180 --> 21:53.010
Tsuzuki strayed from the
course and lost control.

21:53.110 --> 21:58.210
But he had warmly protected me
without touching my past.

21:58.320 --> 22:01.520
So this time, I will...

22:01.790 --> 22:10.410
Episode 13   The Kyoto Arc, Part 4

22:01.790 --> 22:05.520
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The Kyoto Arc, Part 4.

22:06.060 --> 22:09.550
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
I wait for you on the street corner

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
